Body:
@nexxeln @rekram1-node, this PR adds a bounded stderr listener to the MCP stdio transport so that startup errors from local servers are surfaced in the error status instead of being silently lost. It fixes #35719 (assigned to @nexxeln) and also addresses the root cause of #34271 (piped stderr with no reader).

Note: PR #37634 addresses a related but different problem (draining stderr to prevent pipe blockage on Windows), it discards the content. This PR captures it for diagnostics. The two are complementary.

Would appreciate a review when you get a chance.

I’m running into the same issue.

The Codex (currently ChatGPT) app provides a much cleaner experience here: invoking a skill only adds a lightweight skill reference or metadata entry to the visible conversation, while the agent can still access the full skill instructions internally.

In OpenCode, I currently avoid invoking skills explicitly. Instead, I mention the skill name in a normal message and let the agent load it automatically. This keeps the conversation readable, but it is an inconvenient workaround.

Ideally, explicit skill invocation should:

* display only the skill name and description in the user message;
* keep the complete `SKILL.md` content available to the agent;
* optionally allow users to expand the full content;
* avoid rendering the skill instructions as if they were written by the user.

In other words, the visible conversation representation should be separated from the context supplied to the agent.
